1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:02,665
Okay.

2
00:00:02,685 --> 00:00:04,793
Let's back up.

3
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:07,339
Ten hours earlier.

4
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:12,111
What if you woke up in a world where zombies only come out at night…

5
00:00:12,131 --> 00:00:18,188
and you had exactly ten hours, with nothing but your bare hands, to build a home they can't get into?

6
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:20,898
Rule one: the sun keeps time.

7
00:00:20,918 --> 00:00:26,633
Rule two: everything you need is somewhere in this meadow.

8
00:00:26,653 --> 00:00:29,836
Rule three: when the sun touches the horizon…

9
00:00:29,856 --> 00:00:31,145
they come.

10
00:00:31,165 --> 00:00:33,502
Let's see what you can build.

11
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:38,366
First problem: you can't build anything without tools.

12
00:00:38,386 --> 00:00:39,872
You look around.

13
00:00:39,892 --> 00:00:42,745
Trees, grass, rocks, more grass.

14
00:00:42,765 --> 00:00:50,433
So you grab the best tool in the whole meadow, a nice sturdy stick, and give that tree everything you've got.

15
00:00:50,453 --> 00:00:52,960
And now your only tool is…

16
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:53,224
was…

17
00:00:53,244 --> 00:00:53,922
a stick.

18
00:00:54,483 --> 00:00:58,116
So you do what every survivor in history has done.

19
00:00:58,136 --> 00:01:00,672
You hit a rock with a rock.

20
00:01:00,692 --> 00:01:01,254
The rock…

21
00:01:01,274 --> 00:01:01,901
hits back.

22
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:04,316
Your teeth are still buzzing.

23
00:01:04,336 --> 00:01:09,511
But on the fourth try it splits, and suddenly you're holding a sharp edge.

24
00:01:09,531 --> 00:01:15,244
Tie it to a branch with some vine, and congratulations: you've invented the axe.

25
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:18,978
With an axe, a tree takes minutes, not hours.

26
00:01:18,998 --> 00:01:20,905
One tree, two trees, five.

27
00:01:20,925 --> 00:01:24,242
Every log is a wall, a beam, a spike for later.

28
00:01:24,262 --> 00:01:27,100
And while you're at it, a wooden shield.

29
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,256
Is it good?

30
00:01:28,276 --> 00:01:28,501
No.

31
00:01:28,521 --> 00:01:31,799
Is it better than nothing?

32
00:01:31,819 --> 00:01:32,474
Absolutely.

33
00:01:32,494 --> 00:01:35,296
Two hours down, and you've got gear.

34
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:40,287
Here's what nobody tells you: where you build matters more than what you build.

35
00:01:40,307 --> 00:01:43,691
Tall grass hides them until they're on top of you.

36
00:01:43,711 --> 00:01:46,113
Open fields mean they come from every direction.

37
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:49,387
But a little hill with giant boulders at your back?

38
00:01:49,407 --> 00:01:53,633
They can only come from one side, and from up here, you'll see them coming.

39
00:01:54,633 --> 00:01:58,194
Foundation first, made of stone, so nothing digs underneath.

40
00:01:58,214 --> 00:02:01,390
Then the frame: four corner posts, buried deep.

41
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:04,754
Then the walls, log by log, gaps packed with mud.

42
00:02:04,774 --> 00:02:12,327
Then a proper roof, because if every zombie movie has taught you anything, it's never sleep somewhere they can drop in.

43
00:02:12,347 --> 00:02:17,614
Four hours in, and for the first time, you have somewhere that's yours.

44
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,350
You need more stone, so you start chipping at the boulders.

45
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:24,354
And that's when you find it.

46
00:02:24,374 --> 00:02:27,148
A crack, and something glowing inside.

47
00:02:27,168 --> 00:02:29,393
A crystal that shines on its own.

48
00:02:29,413 --> 00:02:35,739
In a world where the monsters come out in the dark, a light that never runs out isn't treasure.

49
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:36,496
It's a weapon.

50
00:02:36,516 --> 00:02:39,461
Lash a shard to a long pole: crystal spear.

51
00:02:39,481 --> 00:02:43,395
Strap leather and scrap metal to your arms and legs: armour.

52
00:02:43,415 --> 00:02:43,935
It's ugly.

53
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:44,820
It squeaks.

54
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,639
You love it.

55
00:02:46,183 --> 00:02:47,050
Seven hours gone.

56
00:02:47,070 --> 00:02:49,084
You've got a house, a spear and armour.

57
00:02:49,104 --> 00:02:49,554
Honestly?

58
00:02:49,574 --> 00:02:51,322
You're feeling pretty good.

59
00:02:51,342 --> 00:02:53,329
You even have time to sit down.

60
00:02:53,349 --> 00:02:54,584
But look around.

61
00:02:54,604 --> 00:02:56,248
A house isn't a fortress.

62
00:02:56,268 --> 00:02:59,559
There's nothing between those walls and the open meadow.

63
00:02:59,579 --> 00:03:04,697
And when the sun goes down, you're going to find out about the one thing you got wrong.

64
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:09,537
Step one of turning a house into a fortress: make it hurt to touch.

65
00:03:09,557 --> 00:03:16,459
You sharpen every log you have left and hammer them in a ring around the cabin, every single point facing out.

66
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:19,791
Anything that wants in has to go through them.

67
00:03:19,811 --> 00:03:21,677
Then a trench, outside the spikes.

68
00:03:21,697 --> 00:03:24,802
It won't stop them, but it slows them down.

69
00:03:24,822 --> 00:03:27,358
And slow zombies are zombies you can count.

70
00:03:27,917 --> 00:03:34,003
You still need a way in and out, so: a drawbridge over the trench, held up with rope.

71
00:03:34,023 --> 00:03:34,866
Well.

72
00:03:34,886 --> 00:03:35,474
Vine rope.

73
00:03:35,494 --> 00:03:37,528
You give it a tug.

74
00:03:37,548 --> 00:03:38,757
It'll hold.

75
00:03:38,777 --> 00:03:39,534
…Probably.

76
00:03:40,083 --> 00:03:44,343
Up on the roof: a lookout, and arrows tipped with that glowing crystal.

77
00:03:44,363 --> 00:03:48,324
Every shot is a flare, and every flare shows you where they are.

78
00:03:48,344 --> 00:03:54,773
And one last thing: a boulder hanging over your front door, for when every other plan fails.

79
00:03:54,793 --> 00:03:57,996
You really hope you never need it.

80
00:03:58,016 --> 00:03:59,956
Then the sun touches the horizon.

81
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,002
The music stops.

82
00:04:03,022 --> 00:04:04,787
Even the bugs go quiet.

83
00:04:04,807 --> 00:04:07,231
You hold your breath and listen.

84
00:04:07,251 --> 00:04:08,602
Nothing.

85
00:04:08,622 --> 00:04:10,630
Then one pair of eyes.

86
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:11,789
Then ten.

87
00:04:11,809 --> 00:04:13,744
Then you stop counting.

88
00:04:13,764 --> 00:04:15,028
They don't run.

89
00:04:15,048 --> 00:04:16,123
They don't need to.

90
00:04:16,143 --> 00:04:18,368
They know you're not going anywhere.

91
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:21,758
The first ones hit the trench and tumble in.

92
00:04:21,778 --> 00:04:25,266
The ones behind climb right over them, straight into the spikes.

93
00:04:25,286 --> 00:04:31,822
And every crystal arrow lights up the dark for a heartbeat, so you know exactly where they are.

94
00:04:31,842 --> 00:04:32,041
One.

95
00:04:32,061 --> 00:04:32,630
Two.

96
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:32,904
Five.

97
00:04:32,924 --> 00:04:34,450
The walls are holding.

98
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:36,993
Everything you built today is working.

99
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:39,941
Then, just like that, they pull back.

100
00:04:39,961 --> 00:04:42,934
For a moment, you actually think you've won.

101
00:04:42,954 --> 00:04:46,747
And then the pebbles on the roof start to bounce.

102
00:04:46,767 --> 00:04:48,149
The ground is shaking.

103
00:04:49,133 --> 00:04:50,538
Something big is coming.

104
00:04:50,558 --> 00:04:52,320
It doesn't stop at the trench.

105
00:04:52,340 --> 00:04:54,279
It doesn't care about the spikes.

106
00:04:54,299 --> 00:04:56,851
It goes straight for the gate.

107
00:04:56,871 --> 00:04:58,946
And the drawbridge rope…

108
00:04:58,966 --> 00:04:59,777
the vine rope.

109
00:04:59,797 --> 00:05:00,871
Of course.

110
00:05:00,891 --> 00:05:03,886
It was always going to be the vine rope.

111
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:05,248
They're inside.

112
00:05:05,268 --> 00:05:06,065
No more arrows.

113
00:05:06,085 --> 00:05:06,611
Spear out.

114
00:05:06,631 --> 00:05:13,081
You jump down, off the wall, duck, spin, back to the doorway, because if they get through that door, it's over.

115
00:05:13,101 --> 00:05:17,881
One of them lands a hit, and that armour you almost didn't bother making?

116
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,359
It just saved your life.

117
00:05:19,917 --> 00:05:21,322
But there are too many.

118
00:05:21,342 --> 00:05:23,428
Back up the ladder, onto the roof.

119
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:25,167
Nowhere left to run.

120
00:05:25,187 --> 00:05:29,305
The big one is right below you, at the front door.

121
00:05:29,325 --> 00:05:30,713
Just one rope…

122
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:31,874
and one boulder.

123
00:05:32,367 --> 00:05:33,614
Goodbye, big guy.

124
00:05:33,634 --> 00:05:36,452
And right on cue…

125
00:05:36,472 --> 00:05:37,538
sunrise.

126
00:05:37,558 --> 00:05:42,234
Every one of them the light touches crumbles into ash.

127
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,131
You made it.

128
00:05:45,151 --> 00:05:46,094
One night.

129
00:05:46,114 --> 00:05:50,571
The gate is gone, your spear is chipped, and you can't feel your arms.

130
00:05:50,591 --> 00:05:55,150
But the sun is already moving again, and tonight, they'll come back bigger.

131
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:57,792
So, what would you build first?

132
00:05:57,812 --> 00:05:59,454
Tell me in the comments.

133
00:05:59,474 --> 00:06:01,594
And if you want to see night two…

134
00:06:01,614 --> 00:06:03,249
you know what to do.

